WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:02.502
-My first guests are
the co-anchors

00:00:02.502 --> 00:00:05.405
of "Weekend Update"
on "Saturday Night Live,"

00:00:05.405 --> 00:00:07.540
which returns this Saturday,

00:00:07.540 --> 00:00:11.111
with host Chris Rock and musical
guest Megan Thee Stallion.

00:00:11.111 --> 00:00:13.646
Let me introduce, please...
[ Drum roll ]

00:00:13.646 --> 00:00:15.381
Michael Che!

00:00:15.381 --> 00:00:16.482
[ Applause ]

00:00:16.482 --> 00:00:18.751
-♪ Michael Che and Colin Jost ♪

00:00:18.751 --> 00:00:20.519
♪♪

00:00:20.519 --> 00:00:22.455
♪ Sit on down,
talk to the host ♪

00:00:22.455 --> 00:00:24.190
-Thank you for being here.
Thank you.

00:00:24.190 --> 00:00:25.759
♪♪

00:00:25.759 --> 00:00:27.193
-Yeah!

00:00:27.193 --> 00:00:29.395
And he's also
a "New York Times"

00:00:29.395 --> 00:00:31.231
best-selling author.

00:00:31.231 --> 00:00:35.334
Please welcome Colin Jost,
everybody!

00:00:35.334 --> 00:00:39.371
-♪ Michael Che and Colin Jost ♪
[ Applause ]

00:00:39.371 --> 00:00:42.375
♪ Sit on down,
talk to the host ♪

00:00:42.375 --> 00:00:44.076
♪♪

00:00:44.076 --> 00:00:47.446
♪ From a distance,
you will sit ♪

00:00:47.446 --> 00:00:50.182
[ Applause and laughter ]

00:00:50.182 --> 00:00:52.018
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:00:52.018 --> 00:00:54.721
-Thank you for being here.
This is fantastic.

00:00:54.721 --> 00:00:56.689
-Thanks for having us, man.
-Yeah, this is cool.

00:00:56.689 --> 00:00:57.991
-Yeah, this is nice.

00:00:57.991 --> 00:01:00.193
-Thank you for being
our first...

00:01:00.193 --> 00:01:02.929
[ Laughter ]

00:01:02.929 --> 00:01:07.000
...two-person in-studio
guests, you know?

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:08.801
Uh...

00:01:08.801 --> 00:01:11.004
I'm sorry.

00:01:11.004 --> 00:01:12.805
Colin, I'm sorry.
I just --

00:01:12.805 --> 00:01:14.407
You -- I mean, you...

00:01:14.407 --> 00:01:17.243
[ Laughter ]

00:01:17.243 --> 00:01:20.680
Do you -- do you feel
far away?

00:01:20.680 --> 00:01:23.416
-I don't feel far away.

00:01:23.416 --> 00:01:28.254
I -- I am farther away.
I'm a lot farther away.

00:01:28.254 --> 00:01:31.157
-Yeah, well, this is for
protocol and all that stuff,

00:01:31.157 --> 00:01:33.159
so I just, you know...
Can you --

00:01:33.159 --> 00:01:34.627
-I can't hear anything
you're saying.

00:01:34.627 --> 00:01:36.195
[ Laughter ]

00:01:36.195 --> 00:01:39.532
-Thank you for coming
on the show, appreciate it!

00:01:39.532 --> 00:01:41.801
-Yeah, anytime, man.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:41.801 --> 00:01:44.504
-New normal!
-Uh, yeah.

00:01:44.504 --> 00:01:46.172
-We're back in 30 Rock.

00:01:46.172 --> 00:01:48.073
-Yeah, man, this is exciting,
dude.

00:01:48.073 --> 00:01:49.409
-I think I saw you
at the tests

00:01:49.409 --> 00:01:52.378
when we were doing all the,
uh, nose swab real quick

00:01:52.378 --> 00:01:54.012
the first day we were, but --

00:01:54.012 --> 00:01:57.150
How's it like working six feet
apart from each other?

00:01:57.150 --> 00:01:59.052
-I love it, I owe a lot
of people money.

00:01:59.052 --> 00:02:00.653
[ Laughter ]

00:02:00.653 --> 00:02:02.121
Nobody can get it from me.

00:02:02.121 --> 00:02:03.957
[ Laughter ]

00:02:03.957 --> 00:02:06.092
-Just enough apart, yeah.
-It's perfect.

00:02:06.092 --> 00:02:07.927
-Are they making
changes to 8H?

00:02:07.927 --> 00:02:10.396
What's happening on Studio 8H?

00:02:10.396 --> 00:02:13.132
-We haven't really been in yet
and seen what it is, right?

00:02:13.132 --> 00:02:15.401
We had our table read.
-Yeah.

00:02:15.401 --> 00:02:17.002
-What was that like?

00:02:17.002 --> 00:02:20.640
-Well, we have 20 cast members
in our show right now,

00:02:20.640 --> 00:02:22.341
and they have to be
six feet apart.

00:02:22.341 --> 00:02:24.844
So 20 times 6 is probably
like a thousand.

00:02:24.844 --> 00:02:26.379
I don't know.
-Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:02:26.379 --> 00:02:28.981
So you're in a table read
and you're hearing voices

00:02:28.981 --> 00:02:30.483
and you're like,
"Who said that"?

00:02:30.483 --> 00:02:31.584
-Yeah.

00:02:31.584 --> 00:02:32.785
-You're like looking around.
-No way.

00:02:32.785 --> 00:02:34.320
-It's a great time for crew
to yell stuff,

00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:35.622
because people will be like,

00:02:35.622 --> 00:02:37.489
"I guess they're just
in the cast. It's fine."

00:02:37.489 --> 00:02:39.492
-Yeah, it feels like you're
listening to a podcast.

00:02:39.492 --> 00:02:40.993
You just --
you don't see anybody.

00:02:40.993 --> 00:02:43.495
-"No, we're all here," yeah.
-It's great. It's kind of cool.

00:02:43.495 --> 00:02:45.831
-That's bizarre.
-It is, but it's, you know.

00:02:45.831 --> 00:02:48.100
-What will the audience
look like?

00:02:48.100 --> 00:02:49.769
-What are you guys talking
about over there?

00:02:49.769 --> 00:02:51.737
-We're talking about
"Saturday Night Live"!

00:02:51.737 --> 00:02:53.206
-Oh, that's great.
-Coming back this weekend.

00:02:53.206 --> 00:02:55.174
-That's great.
-I was like,

00:02:55.174 --> 00:02:57.209
what is the audience
going to be like?

00:02:57.209 --> 00:02:58.778
-White.
-No, no --

00:02:58.778 --> 00:03:00.046
[ Laughter ]

00:03:00.046 --> 00:03:01.213
No, no, no.

00:03:01.213 --> 00:03:02.949
-To start with,
they're all white.

00:03:02.949 --> 00:03:04.317
-No, no, no, no.

00:03:04.317 --> 00:03:05.985
-I don't know if you're
a fan, but...

00:03:05.985 --> 00:03:07.453
[ Laughter ]

00:03:07.453 --> 00:03:09.088
-Everybody enjoys that show.

00:03:09.088 --> 00:03:12.525
But, I mean, is it going to
change the style for "Update"?

00:03:12.525 --> 00:03:15.160
Are you gonna still do it the
way you guys have been doing it?

00:03:15.160 --> 00:03:16.429
Well, you got to be safe.

00:03:16.429 --> 00:03:18.564
-It's a maximum capacity of one
at the desk.

00:03:18.564 --> 00:03:20.099
-Congratulations, Colin.

00:03:20.099 --> 00:03:21.901
Yeah, we get "Update"
with Colin Jost.

00:03:21.901 --> 00:03:23.436
-Sorry.
-I'm all for it.

00:03:23.436 --> 00:03:24.904
[ Laughter ]

00:03:24.904 --> 00:03:26.705
As long as I get paid
the same, it's fine with me.

00:03:26.705 --> 00:03:28.007
No, it should be fun.

00:03:28.007 --> 00:03:30.876
I think it's actually
more fun.

00:03:30.876 --> 00:03:32.578
Rules make comedy fun,

00:03:32.578 --> 00:03:34.713
When there's things you can't
do, when there's kind of

00:03:34.713 --> 00:03:37.483
loopholes, that's when you start
to really get creative,

00:03:37.483 --> 00:03:40.320
and I think the show is kind of
the perfect place for that.

00:03:40.320 --> 00:03:41.453
-Yeah.
-That was like

00:03:41.453 --> 00:03:42.822
the political answer.

00:03:42.822 --> 00:03:44.557
-No, that was a great answer.
I agree with you.

00:03:44.557 --> 00:03:46.059
I love rules.

00:03:46.059 --> 00:03:47.860
[ Laughter ]
-I love rules.

00:03:47.860 --> 00:03:49.562
-I do, I love it, because
I like to break them.

00:03:49.562 --> 00:03:51.064
I go, yeah, go ahead,
tell me what I can't do,

00:03:51.064 --> 00:03:53.166
and I'll find a way something.
-Yeah.

00:03:53.166 --> 00:03:57.103
You have the best host
for the first show back,

00:03:57.103 --> 00:03:59.405
and it is Chris Rock.
And I heard --

00:03:59.405 --> 00:04:00.973
We had Chris on the show
and he told me

00:04:00.973 --> 00:04:03.208
that you guys had to
actually go to his house

00:04:03.208 --> 00:04:05.278
and convince him.
-Oh, yeah.

00:04:05.278 --> 00:04:07.413
We literally went
to Chris Rock's house

00:04:07.413 --> 00:04:11.217
to tell him to do "SNL,"
and it was very --

00:04:11.217 --> 00:04:12.952
It felt like that scene
in "The Godfather,"

00:04:12.952 --> 00:04:15.989
remember when Tom Hagen
goes to tell the guy

00:04:15.989 --> 00:04:17.523
to put the dude in the movie?
-Yeah.

00:04:17.523 --> 00:04:18.825
-I've never seen
"The Godfather,"

00:04:18.825 --> 00:04:20.359
but someone told me
it was similar.

00:04:20.359 --> 00:04:21.961
[ Laughter ]

00:04:21.961 --> 00:04:23.662
I might have gotten
bad information, Jimmy.

00:04:23.662 --> 00:04:25.231
But...
-Tom Hagen.

00:04:25.231 --> 00:04:26.465
That's a deep cut.

00:04:26.465 --> 00:04:27.900
-Oh, yeah, but that's
what it felt like.

00:04:27.900 --> 00:04:29.268
I was like, literally like,
"How could you not --

00:04:29.268 --> 00:04:30.869
You got to do it, man.
It's New York City.

00:04:30.869 --> 00:04:32.171
We're back. It's 30 Rock.

00:04:32.171 --> 00:04:34.573
You got to come home
and we got to make people,

00:04:34.573 --> 00:04:36.642
you know, feel good again."
-Yeah.

00:04:36.642 --> 00:04:38.878
The country wants this.
The country needs it.

00:04:38.878 --> 00:04:40.312
I will be watching it.
I cannot wait.

00:04:40.312 --> 00:04:42.582
More with Michael Che and
Colin Jost when we come back.

